1
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:49,200
Goodbye, Mr. Shi.

2
00:01:51,439 --> 00:01:51,959
How'd it go?

3
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,359
I was right, wasn't I?

4
00:01:54,159 --> 00:01:56,480
They want a proper construction crew.

5
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:57,680
What your dad has...

6
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,439
...is basically just a family workshop.

7
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:00,959
It's actually good that he stepped back.

8
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,359
He's getting on in years anyway,

9
00:02:02,359 --> 00:02:03,319
and his health isn't so good.

10
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:12,599
So,

11
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,879
why did you go to the construction site today?

12
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,120
I'm asking you, why did you go there?

13
00:02:19,599 --> 00:02:20,639
You haven't gone there in ages.

14
00:02:24,719 --> 00:02:25,439
Well...

15
00:02:26,879 --> 00:02:27,919
Come on, sit down first.

16
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,240
Let's agree on something first.

17
00:02:31,719 --> 00:02:32,560
No getting mad.

18
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:34,800
Just say it.

19
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:42,800
The old man gave me the ledger.

20
00:02:42,879 --> 00:02:43,360
What?

21
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,080
Didn't we just agree...

22
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:46,199
not to get mad?

23
00:02:54,759 --> 00:02:55,840
Can you stop counting already?

24
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,400
Just go to sleep.

25
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:58,840
When I get up tomorrow,

26
00:02:58,840 --> 00:02:59,840
I still have to go to the site.

27
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:00,599
What site?

28
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:02,039
Didn't I tell you

29
00:03:02,039 --> 00:03:02,800
not to go?

30
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:03,919
Let Sai Xiuliang go from now on.

31
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:05,120
That won't work!

32
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:05,960
He doesn't know anything.

33
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:06,800
How can we let him go?

34
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,840
Doesn't your dad favor him?

35
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,639
I'd like to see how he runs things.

36
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,800
Let's see in three days

37
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:12,159
what this site turns into.

38
00:03:14,879 --> 00:03:15,400
Look, honey,

39
00:03:15,599 --> 00:03:17,479
isn't that totally redundant?

40
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,719
In the end,

41
00:03:19,039 --> 00:03:20,120
I'll still have to deal with it.

42
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:21,520
Isn't that just asking for trouble?

43
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,000
Just let him sign off on it, and we're done.

44
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
What are you talking about?

45
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:25,479
Who does the construction crew belong to?

46
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:26,280
Is it yours,

47
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,000
or Sai Xiuliang's?

48
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,439
Don't tell me it belongs to the Sai family.

49
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,800
Let me tell you, Sai Xiuming.

50
00:03:30,159 --> 00:03:30,919
While your dad is around,

51
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,479
this family still counts as one.

52
00:03:32,919 --> 00:03:34,039
Once your dad is gone,

53
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:35,800
who'll call the shots, you or Sai Xiuliang?

54
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:36,560
Have you ever thought about that?

55
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:38,479
Honey,

56
00:03:39,599 --> 00:03:40,479
you probably don't even realize it,

57
00:03:40,759 --> 00:03:42,360
but whenever you mention Dad and my brother,

58
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,319
your whole face scrunches up.

59
00:03:45,039 --> 00:03:45,879
Back when I married you,

60
00:03:45,879 --> 00:03:48,319
you were so pretty and gentle.

61
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:48,960
Gentle?

62
00:03:50,199 --> 00:03:51,520
Being gentle requires capital.

63
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,400
If I were holding 14 million today,

64
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,719
I'd be gentle for the whole world to see!

65
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,280
I'd let everyone know how gentle I am.

66
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:59,280
But right now, I have nothing.

67
00:03:59,719 --> 00:04:00,479
For food and clothes,

68
00:04:00,479 --> 00:04:01,560
I have to rely on handouts.

69
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:03,000
If I try to get a single cent from the site,

70
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,520
I have to bend to your dad's and brother's whims.

71
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:05,960
My gentleness isn't gentleness.

72
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,120
It's called weakness!

73
00:04:07,439 --> 00:04:08,719
You think I'm just some persimmon here?

74
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:09,599
Well, persimmons can be firm, too—

75
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:10,400
not just Pushovers!

76
00:04:12,479 --> 00:04:13,680
Your dad is really something.

77
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:15,919
He just assumed that right now,

78
00:04:15,919 --> 00:04:16,879
you wouldn't say no to him.

79
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:18,800
He has you wrapped around his finger.

80
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,600
Look at the mess you're in right now!

81
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:23,240
On one hand, you take Tengyue's consulting fees,

82
00:04:23,839 --> 00:04:24,720
while Shi Yongnian

83
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,639
wants to kick out teams like your dad's.

84
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:29,519
On the other hand, you take your dad's ledger

85
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,040
to protect the team for him.

86
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:31,639
Tell me,

87
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,560
whose side are you really on?

88
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,079
Wasn't that before?

89
00:04:35,079 --> 00:04:37,519
I didn't know he was kicking out the team then.

90
00:04:37,839 --> 00:04:38,560
Besides, this...

91
00:04:38,959 --> 00:04:40,519
didn't you see Uncle Ma's condition?

92
00:04:40,519 --> 00:04:41,360
This ledger, indeed...

93
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,480
I had to take it.

94
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,439
Can you even handle it?

95
00:04:43,439 --> 00:04:43,959
How are you going to manage?

96
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,839
Your law firm just opened,

97
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,319
and there's a ton of work to do.

98
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:48,519
Where will you find the energy?

99
00:04:48,639 --> 00:04:50,399
Besides, you can't even read this ledger!

100
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,439
If you ask me,

101
00:04:52,399 --> 00:04:53,160
you should give it to someone else.

102
00:04:54,199 --> 00:04:55,439
Give it to whom?

103
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:57,000
To Sai Xiuming or Wen Jiayin!

104
00:04:57,639 --> 00:04:59,199
That would be completely irresponsible.

105
00:04:59,319 --> 00:05:01,040
The old man simply doesn't trust them.

106
00:05:01,319 --> 00:05:02,519
That's why he went to all this trouble

107
00:05:02,519 --> 00:05:03,399
to have Uncle Ma hand it to me.

108
00:05:03,399 --> 00:05:04,160
He was also thinking,

109
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,560
what if he doesn't make it out of surgery?

110
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,040
What happens to his business then?

111
00:05:06,279 --> 00:05:07,160
That's why he wanted the ledger

112
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,360
in the hands of the person he trusts most.

113
00:05:08,439 --> 00:05:09,240
So what do you mean?

114
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,920
You're dead set on dealing with this?

115
00:05:11,199 --> 00:05:12,120
Dragging yourself into the mess?

116
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,240
No, no, no, that's not it.

117
00:05:14,079 --> 00:05:14,879
It's just temporary.

118
00:05:14,879 --> 00:05:15,600
Temporary?

119
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:16,959
Temporary for how long?

120
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:18,439
Did you forget Mid-Autumn Festival,

121
00:05:18,439 --> 00:05:19,800
when your dad slapped you across the face?

122
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,560
Now he suddenly remembers you,

123
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:23,560
making you take the fall,

124
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,120
roasting you over an open fire!

125
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,439
What do you call this?

126
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,319
It's called: Never learns a lesson!

127
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,360
You barely dragged yourself

128
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:31,480
out of that quagmire,

129
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,199
and now you're jumping right back in!

130
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,800
Don't you dare be so foolish!

131
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,560
Fine, fine, fine.

132
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,480
Just hold onto your money

133
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:41,240
and do whatever you want.

134
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:41,759
Happy now?

135
00:05:42,199 --> 00:05:42,759
Can we go to sleep now?

136
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,560
Oh, so I'm actually allowed

137
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,959
to do whatever I want?

138
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,199
Let me think about what I don't want to do first!

139
00:05:48,759 --> 00:05:50,879
I don't want my man doing thankless work!

140
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:52,800
I don't want to spend a single cent

141
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,920
and have to clear it with Sai Xiuliang!

142
00:05:54,079 --> 00:05:55,800
I don't want to wait on Sai Qianjin's dad for her!

143
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,160
I don't want every penny I earn

144
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,319
to need your dad's approval!

145
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,199
All right, that's enough.

146
00:05:59,399 --> 00:06:00,000
That's enough!

147
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:01,720
Stop nagging, will you?

148
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,240
If I don't get that ledger back,

149
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,680
my name isn't Wen Jiayin!

150
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,279
Let go!

151
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:12,040
I gotta pee!

152
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:17,680
Where's my jacket?

153
00:06:17,959 --> 00:06:18,360
I don't know.

154
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:35,319
Have you seen my jacket?

155
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,519
Did I leave it at your place?

156
00:06:37,079 --> 00:06:37,879
Your jacket?

157
00:06:40,319 --> 00:06:41,079
Let me check.

158
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:45,759
Doesn't look like it.

159
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,040
Well, never mind then.

160
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:48,560
Probably left it at the construction site.

161
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,079
I'll keep looking.

162
00:06:49,439 --> 00:06:49,959
Thanks, thanks.

163
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:50,519
All right.

164
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:37,240
Big Brother, hurry up, you two!

165
00:07:37,279 --> 00:07:38,399
I'll take them to the car and wait for you.

166
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:39,120
Coming, coming!

167
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:43,600
Wait for me!

168
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:44,319
You're walking so fast!

169
00:07:44,439 --> 00:07:44,959
What is it?

170
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,439
Don't go today.

171
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,040
Just don't go.

172
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:48,360
Wait, what?

173
00:07:48,839 --> 00:07:50,800
You always say I'm so slow I'd even miss out on warm shit.

174
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:52,720
Today Dad's moving from the ICU to a regular ward.

175
00:07:52,959 --> 00:07:53,759
At a crucial moment like this, I...

176
00:07:54,079 --> 00:07:54,759
Why wouldn't I go?

177
00:07:54,759 --> 00:07:55,360
I told you not to go,

178
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,040
so don't go!

179
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,279
Just stay put at the construction site.

180
00:07:57,759 --> 00:07:59,120
Send Dad a text to check in,

181
00:07:59,240 --> 00:07:59,959
and say you're busy at the site.

182
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,279
Wait, what kind of game are you playing?

183
00:08:02,279 --> 00:08:02,839
Whatever game it is,

184
00:08:02,839 --> 00:08:03,600
we have to play the opposite tune.

185
00:08:04,279 --> 00:08:05,360
Take a page from Second Brother's book.

186
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,199
When he's supposed to show up,

187
00:08:06,199 --> 00:08:06,879
he acts aloof and says he can't make it.

188
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:07,800
He says he won't come,

189
00:08:07,879 --> 00:08:08,959
then bam, drops in out of nowhere,

190
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:09,879
all huffing and puffing,

191
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,240
making sure everyone notices him!

192
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,519
Why should we be the honest fools,

193
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,639
playing by Dad's script every single time?

194
00:08:15,199 --> 00:08:15,839
You're not allowed to go.

195
00:08:16,439 --> 00:08:16,879
Don't you go.

196
00:08:19,639 --> 00:08:20,279
Coming!

197
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:41,600
Grandpa, you've lost weight.

198
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,480
But your beard didn't stop growing.

199
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,639
Grandpa had surgery, he has incisions.

200
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,320
It hurts.

201
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,519
His flesh hurts, not his beard.

202
00:08:51,519 --> 00:08:51,840
Dad.

203
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,279
I'm planning to apply to medical school.

204
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:58,759
Dad...

205
00:08:59,519 --> 00:09:00,480
If you're in pain,

206
00:09:00,799 --> 00:09:02,519
there's a pain pump on your left.

207
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,559
Turn it up a bit.

208
00:09:03,639 --> 00:09:04,440
Don't just tough it out.

209
00:09:05,399 --> 00:09:05,720
Dad.

210
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:06,519
Dad.

211
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:16,519
Dad.

212
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:18,440
Dad.

213
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:20,919
Looking for Xiuming?

214
00:09:22,679 --> 00:09:23,639
He's at the construction site.

215
00:09:23,799 --> 00:09:25,399
His phone's been ringing off the hook all morning.

216
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,600
Don't worry.

217
00:09:29,519 --> 00:09:30,919
It's business as usual,

218
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,679
but with you not around,

219
00:09:33,879 --> 00:09:34,840
he's having a tough time.

220
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,039
Big Brother too...

221
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:39,759
After working all these years,

222
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:42,039
what's the big fuss?

223
00:09:42,039 --> 00:09:42,879
What's the big emergency

224
00:09:42,879 --> 00:09:44,240
that it has to be dealt with first thing in the morning?

225
00:09:45,679 --> 00:09:46,039
Dad,

226
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:47,919
you know what Xiuming is like

227
00:09:47,919 --> 00:09:49,000
better than anyone.

228
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,080
He's honest to a fault.

229
00:09:50,799 --> 00:09:53,120
He always puts others first.

230
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,759
If payments aren't settled promptly,

231
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,120
he worries it'll put people in a bind.

232
00:09:57,480 --> 00:09:59,039
Payments do need to be handled carefully.

233
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,840
Big Brother is an old hand on the job site,

234
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,759
yet he still gets so worked up.

235
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:04,559
Xiuliang,

236
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,080
you're a rich man.

237
00:10:07,519 --> 00:10:09,000
You don't understand job site business.

238
00:10:09,759 --> 00:10:11,279
Construction work requires a conscience.

239
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,159
Everyone's got families to feed.

240
00:10:14,679 --> 00:10:15,320
Right, Dad?

241
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:15,919
Well,

242
00:10:17,399 --> 00:10:19,600
Sai Duoxi survived a grave illness,

243
00:10:20,159 --> 00:10:21,960
but the world keeps turning.

244
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:24,639
The people are the same old faces,

245
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,919
and the drama is the same old show.

246
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,440
His blessings

247
00:10:29,919 --> 00:10:31,200
are truly something else.

248
00:10:37,519 --> 00:10:38,080
Changing the dressing?

249
00:10:41,759 --> 00:10:42,559
It's that expensive?

250
00:10:44,559 --> 00:10:45,639
Is the ICU really this expensive?

251
00:10:46,399 --> 00:10:46,960
Dad didn't even do anything,

252
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:48,240
and one night cost 5,000 or 6,000?

253
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:49,039
How much?

254
00:10:51,919 --> 00:10:52,440
Holy crap!

255
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,600
45,000?

256
00:10:53,879 --> 00:10:54,519
More than that.

257
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,519
We still owe over 10,000 on the deposit.

258
00:10:56,679 --> 00:10:57,720
That's over 50,000 in total.

259
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:00,039
If I'd known hospitals were such cash cows,

260
00:11:00,639 --> 00:11:01,159
Second Brother,

261
00:11:01,799 --> 00:11:02,879
you shouldn't have opened a law firm.

262
00:11:02,879 --> 00:11:03,960
You should've opened a clinic!

263
00:11:04,879 --> 00:11:06,159
This is the ICU!

264
00:11:07,279 --> 00:11:08,080
Did you think it was a hotel?

265
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:08,519
What?

266
00:11:08,519 --> 00:11:09,519
Did you want them to resuscitate him again

267
00:11:09,519 --> 00:11:10,559
just to make it feel worth the money?

268
00:11:10,559 --> 00:11:10,919
Is that it?

269
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,759
No way.

270
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:12,960
Resuscitation costs extra!

271
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:14,399
Alright, alright, that's enough.

272
00:11:14,639 --> 00:11:15,559
I haven't paid the bill yet.

273
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:16,919
There isn't enough money on Dad's card.

274
00:11:18,159 --> 00:11:19,080
How's that possible?

275
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:20,759
Dad ran a construction crew for so many years.

276
00:11:20,879 --> 00:11:21,639
He doesn't have that much?

277
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:22,679
Sister-in-law, do you buy that?

278
00:11:22,799 --> 00:11:23,840
Dad's a contractor,

279
00:11:24,039 --> 00:11:25,000
not an ATM.

280
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,080
Come on.

281
00:11:26,639 --> 00:11:27,639
When he gave you the card,

282
00:11:27,639 --> 00:11:28,399
what did he say to you?

283
00:11:29,279 --> 00:11:29,840
Nothing much.

284
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:30,840
He didn't say a thing.

285
00:11:31,799 --> 00:11:32,840
Then he meant to spend whatever it takes!

286
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,960
Sister-in-law, the card's empty.

287
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:48,919
Is there cash at home?

288
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:49,480
Couldn't find any.

289
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,600
Let's go, we can't talk here.

290
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:51,399
Let's find a place

291
00:11:51,399 --> 00:11:51,960
and talk it over.

292
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:52,840
Don't talk here.

293
00:11:53,440 --> 00:11:54,039
Outside, outside, outside.

294
00:11:54,039 --> 00:11:54,639
Come on, let's go.

295
00:11:54,639 --> 00:11:55,440
Go ask Jin Jingran

296
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,159
if this amount is right.

297
00:11:56,159 --> 00:11:56,879
I'm not asking him.

298
00:11:56,879 --> 00:11:57,519
Take it and ask yourself.

299
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:58,320
Hurry up.

300
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,000
Zhenzhu, call me when Grandpa's done.

301
00:12:03,759 --> 00:12:04,120
This way.

302
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,000
Do you get it now?

303
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,200
Do you know what's going on?

304
00:12:15,879 --> 00:12:16,559
No idea.

305
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:18,600
What's there to get?

306
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:21,799
I get it.

307
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:23,720
Dad is testing us.

308
00:12:23,879 --> 00:12:25,200
Dad deliberately left

309
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,440
only ten thousand yuan in his card.

310
00:12:26,519 --> 00:12:27,360
Whoever fronts the money

311
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:28,320
is the filial one.

312
00:12:28,519 --> 00:12:29,799
Did I get that right, Second Brother?

313
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:32,080
We need to hurry and pay this money.

314
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:33,480
Aren't we forty thousand yuan short?

315
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:34,679
Leaving Xiao Wu out of this,

316
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,120
the four of us, each family,

317
00:12:36,399 --> 00:12:36,879
ten thousand each.

318
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:37,720
Works?

319
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:38,879
Sure, no problem.

320
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:40,600
Sure, no problem for me either.

321
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,279
Put my ten thousand on your tab.

322
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,080
Front it for me first.

323
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,480
Wait, did you pay me back for last time?

324
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,559
What about the time before that?

325
00:12:45,559 --> 00:12:46,080
Have you ever paid me back?

326
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:46,960
I said put it on my tab.

327
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,200
There has to be a grand total!

328
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:48,840
Come on, Second Brother.

329
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:49,480
Don't mind him.

330
00:12:49,759 --> 00:12:51,240
I happen to have ten thousand on hand.

331
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,320
I'll bring it to you later.

332
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:53,679
If you're so loaded,

333
00:12:53,679 --> 00:12:54,440
why don't you pay it all?

334
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:55,399
You're not hurting for thirty grand.

335
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:56,000
Fine by me.

336
00:12:56,639 --> 00:12:57,200
No problem.

337
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,440
Back in the day, I would have.

338
00:12:59,039 --> 00:12:59,720
And what about now?

339
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:00,960
Do you think I could bring myself

340
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:02,639
to ask Jin Jingran for another dime?

341
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,360
Not everyone is shameless like you.

342
00:13:04,519 --> 00:13:05,279
Hey, look at you.

343
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,440
You have no job and no money,

344
00:13:07,559 --> 00:13:08,279
so why the hell divorce him?

345
00:13:08,279 --> 00:13:08,799
Shut your mouth!

346
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:09,559
Wen Jiayin.

347
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:10,559
What about you?

348
00:13:13,679 --> 00:13:14,799
You all know

349
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,320
your oldest brother

350
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:19,879
makes only three thousand a month.

351
00:13:20,159 --> 00:13:21,200
Dad's living allowance

352
00:13:21,200 --> 00:13:22,799
gets spent clean every month.

353
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,159
We have no spare cash at home.

354
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,240
The only funds left

355
00:13:27,519 --> 00:13:29,440
are in Zhenzhu's piggy bank.

356
00:13:30,159 --> 00:13:31,000
If you ask me,

357
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:32,840
whoever has money

358
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,840
should front it first.

359
00:13:34,519 --> 00:13:36,399
Dad will pay it back anyway.

360
00:13:44,399 --> 00:13:44,960
Fine.

361
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:46,519
Understood.

362
00:13:46,799 --> 00:13:47,159
Got it.

363
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,559
Number Four, you don't need to pay your ten grand.

364
00:13:51,799 --> 00:13:52,679
Give me Dad's card.

365
00:13:52,879 --> 00:13:53,720
I'll figure out the rest.

366
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:56,720
Second Brother.

367
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,240
Can I ask you something?

368
00:13:58,240 --> 00:13:58,600
Shoot.

369
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,360
Dad's bank passbook...

370
00:14:00,519 --> 00:14:01,200
is it with you?

371
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,679
Let me suggest something.

372
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,879
Let's split this money right now.

373
00:14:10,039 --> 00:14:10,799
After we divide it,

374
00:14:11,519 --> 00:14:12,080
this forty thousand,

375
00:14:12,639 --> 00:14:14,320
plus whatever comes next, is on me.

376
00:14:14,639 --> 00:14:15,159
I'll cover it all.

377
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,000
How about that?

378
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,120
At a time like this,

379
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,320
you're still talking about dividing money?

380
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:21,120
Doing something so wicked...

381
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:21,600
I could never do that.

382
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,120
Don't guilt-trip me.

383
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:22,879
Don't drag me down with you!

384
00:14:22,879 --> 00:14:23,559
Who's dragging you down?

385
00:14:23,639 --> 00:14:24,159
Shut up!

386
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:25,759
Unfilial!

387
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:27,360
Dad really...

388
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:28,279
Stop staring.

389
00:14:29,559 --> 00:14:30,440
I just don't get it.

390
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,919
Isn't this just a test?

391
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:32,879
Whoever fronts the money

392
00:14:32,879 --> 00:14:33,519
is the filial one.

393
00:14:33,679 --> 00:14:34,799
Let's divide this money.

394
00:14:35,159 --> 00:14:36,000
Come on, look at me.

395
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,720
I'm Sai Xiuhe, the third Sai son.

396
00:14:38,039 --> 00:14:39,200
See if I'm filial or not!

397
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,279
I'll definitely be more filial than you.

398
00:14:40,639 --> 00:14:41,519
I'll definitely give the most.

399
00:14:41,879 --> 00:14:42,559
How about that?

400
00:14:52,519 --> 00:14:53,080
Xiuliang,

401
00:14:54,399 --> 00:14:55,759
Dad put you in charge of the family.

402
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,080
You have to call the shots.

403
00:15:03,919 --> 00:15:04,360
Second Brother...

404
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,200
Get the hell out of my face.

405
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,559
Dad's dressing should be changed by now.

406
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:33,679
Meifan.

407
00:15:34,279 --> 00:15:35,879
Do you have 40,000 yuan on hand?

408
00:15:35,879 --> 00:15:37,679
Could you transfer it to me for now?

409
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,240
What happened?

410
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,440
My dad is in the hospital.

411
00:15:41,879 --> 00:15:42,679
And for the bill...

412
00:15:43,159 --> 00:15:43,559
we're still short.

413
00:15:43,559 --> 00:15:44,600
We're over 40,000 yuan short right now.

414
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:45,440
Wait.

415
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:47,559
Your dad is having surgery,

416
00:15:47,559 --> 00:15:48,919
didn't he prepare money for it?

417
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,039
I checked his account.

418
00:15:50,919 --> 00:15:51,840
He only has a bit over 10,000 yuan.

419
00:15:53,360 --> 00:15:54,120
It's a long story.

420
00:15:54,399 --> 00:15:55,600
So we have to cover it all?

421
00:15:55,919 --> 00:15:56,559
What about the others?

422
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:57,799
They all say they're broke.

423
00:16:01,039 --> 00:16:02,759
What is wrong with your family?

424
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:04,399
In a major crisis like this,

425
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:05,720
they all act like absentee bosses?

426
00:16:05,919 --> 00:16:06,919
Squeezing only you for money?

427
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,320
Are you the only one named Sai?

428
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:09,840
A family like that,

429
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,000
and your dad still refuses to let it break up.

430
00:16:11,159 --> 00:16:11,799
What for?

431
00:16:11,799 --> 00:16:12,639
Honey, listen to me.

432
00:16:12,879 --> 00:16:14,639
Let's... let's not talk about that.

433
00:16:14,639 --> 00:16:15,759
Can we deal with the emergency first?

434
00:16:15,759 --> 00:16:17,279
My dad is still lying in there.

435
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,080
I can't be like them

436
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,159
and just wash my hands of it.

437
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,159
Honey...

438
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,360
It's not that I don't want to lend it.

439
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,559
It's just we really have no spare cash.

440
00:16:26,879 --> 00:16:28,559
Your law firm has been burning through cash,

441
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,519
and with my little salary,

442
00:16:30,919 --> 00:16:32,240
it barely covers our living expenses.

443
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:33,679
How about this?

444
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:36,799
I'll ask my parents for help.

445
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:39,720
Honey...

446
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:41,559
Don't thank me yet.

447
00:16:42,159 --> 00:16:43,440
I'm only helping you this once.

448
00:16:43,679 --> 00:16:44,519
As for what happens next,

449
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,080
you, Sai Xiuming, and Wen Jiayin

450
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,000
need to have a serious talk.

451
00:16:48,279 --> 00:16:49,759
It can't all fall on you alone.

452
00:16:50,399 --> 00:16:50,919
I know.

453
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:52,200
I know.

454
00:16:53,919 --> 00:16:54,240
Honey,

455
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,039
thank you.

456
00:16:57,519 --> 00:16:57,840
All right.

457
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:58,840
We'll talk when you get back.

458
00:17:17,279 --> 00:17:18,240
Brother Xiuming.

459
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:19,720
The breaker tripped.

460
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,559
I'll go check on it.

461
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,319
Uh, there's water in the living room.

462
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,279
Wait for me a sec.

463
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:25,039
Just relax for now.

464
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:27,720
Look at this...

465
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:35,559
Brother Xiuming,

466
00:18:36,759 --> 00:18:38,160
Big Liu at the village entrance

467
00:18:38,799 --> 00:18:40,160
blew the fuse with his water pump.

468
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:40,880
They're working on it right now,

469
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:41,720
so we'll have to wait a bit.

470
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:48,599
Why don't

471
00:18:49,079 --> 00:18:51,039
we check the books first?

472
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:52,240
The books?

473
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:54,240
Sure, sure, okay.

474
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,720
Here are the recent delivery slips.

475
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:11,279
And this is...

476
00:19:11,559 --> 00:19:13,400
the... the grand total.

477
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,000
Sorry about this, Brother Xiuming.

478
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:24,640
Uncle Duoxi is still in the hospital,

479
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,440
you have to run both construction sites,

480
00:19:26,799 --> 00:19:28,720
and you have to help out at home too.

481
00:19:29,279 --> 00:19:30,640
Did I hold you up?

482
00:19:31,079 --> 00:19:32,079
No, not at all.

483
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:37,319
Well...

484
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:45,839
If the power isn't coming back on,

485
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:47,559
I'll... I'll head back first.

486
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,200
I should head back now.

487
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:51,000
Then...

488
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:53,759
Let me walk you out.

489
00:19:54,839 --> 00:19:55,119
No need.

490
00:19:55,119 --> 00:19:56,519
I'll... I'll pack up my things first.

491
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,039
Just pack my stuff.

492
00:19:58,839 --> 00:19:59,759
Let me help you then.

493
00:20:19,359 --> 00:20:19,680
Jiao,

494
00:20:20,359 --> 00:20:20,640
I...

495
00:20:22,319 --> 00:20:23,359
my jacket...

496
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:25,359
did you...?

497
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:31,400
I really did look for it that day.

498
00:20:31,759 --> 00:20:32,799
My dad's room,

499
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,720
the bathroom, the living room—couldn't find it.

500
00:20:36,079 --> 00:20:38,039
Then I spotted it shoved in a corner.

501
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:39,839
It was so filthy!

502
00:20:39,839 --> 00:20:41,640
I was wondering whose it was.

503
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:43,599
It reeked of sweat.

504
00:20:43,599 --> 00:20:45,000
I figured it had to be yours,

505
00:20:45,359 --> 00:20:46,359
so I washed it.

506
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,480
Brother Xiuming,

507
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,400
you're at the construction site every day,

508
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:50,599
all dirty and smelly.

509
00:20:50,599 --> 00:20:52,000
You've got to change clothes more often!

510
00:20:52,359 --> 00:20:53,000
At the very least,

511
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,039
change every two days.

512
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:55,519
Here.

513
00:20:57,119 --> 00:20:58,119
I washed it clean for you.

514
00:21:01,359 --> 00:21:02,720
I... I'll leave my stuff...

515
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,279
leave it at your place for now.

516
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:06,359
I'm not done with the work here anyway.

517
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:08,279
All right.

518
00:21:14,359 --> 00:21:16,119
Take... take care, Brother Xiuming!

519
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,240
He's recovering quite well.

520
00:21:35,319 --> 00:21:36,119
The surgery was very successful.

521
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,079
Just remind him

522
00:21:38,079 --> 00:21:39,079
that he must get out of bed and walk more.

523
00:21:39,319 --> 00:21:40,319
Got it, I'll tell him.

524
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:42,720
Remind his family to urge him on.

525
00:21:43,319 --> 00:21:43,599
Will do.

526
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,559
What brings you here?

527
00:21:46,559 --> 00:21:47,000
Director Jin.

528
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,440
I just came to see you.

529
00:21:50,799 --> 00:21:51,200
Come on in.

530
00:21:55,359 --> 00:21:56,519
Liu Yan, coming, coming!

531
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:03,960
What's all this?

532
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:05,240
Just a small gift.

533
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,039
A token of our appreciation.

534
00:22:06,119 --> 00:22:07,359
Please don't turn it down.

535
00:22:08,079 --> 00:22:08,920
It's not for you.

536
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:11,400
Old Ma got these supplements for your father-in-law.

537
00:22:11,839 --> 00:22:12,839
Just to show his goodwill.

538
00:22:13,119 --> 00:22:14,079
And it was no trouble to bring along.

539
00:22:15,119 --> 00:22:16,200
I'll thank you on my father's behalf.

540
00:22:17,039 --> 00:22:17,319
Have a seat.

541
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:22,880
You're a medical rep.

542
00:22:23,640 --> 00:22:25,000
Don't say I didn't warn you two.

543
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,200
This is a hospital.

544
00:22:26,279 --> 00:22:27,279
Don't give people a reason to gossip.

545
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:28,839
We have to watch appearances.

546
00:22:29,119 --> 00:22:29,720
What did you want to see me about?

547
00:22:32,359 --> 00:22:32,839
Well, it's like this.

548
00:22:33,079 --> 00:22:33,839
Our company

549
00:22:34,039 --> 00:22:36,079
recently became an agent for an imported German

550
00:22:36,079 --> 00:22:37,799
post-op adjuvant drug for cardiac surgery.

551
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,960
It targets anticoagulation and myocardial repair.

552
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,640
The clinical data looks fantastic.

553
00:22:42,279 --> 00:22:44,640
Compared to what the hospital routinely uses now,

554
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:46,680
it improves efficacy by at least 30 percent.

555
00:22:47,279 --> 00:22:48,599
Could you consider

556
00:22:48,799 --> 00:22:50,640
rolling it out in our department?

557
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:54,559
Look, here's the thing.

558
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,039
For our hospital to adopt a new drug,

559
00:22:56,319 --> 00:22:57,759
there's a strict review process.

560
00:22:58,279 --> 00:22:59,319
It has to be evaluated

561
00:22:59,319 --> 00:23:01,079
by the Pharmacy and Therapeutics Committee.

562
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:03,400
I... I can't decide this on my own.

563
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:04,039
Besides,

564
00:23:04,640 --> 00:23:05,839
the new director hasn't been chosen yet.

565
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:07,359
So,

566
00:23:08,279 --> 00:23:09,160
don't put me in a tough spot.

567
00:23:09,599 --> 00:23:10,559
We know the procedure.

568
00:23:10,880 --> 00:23:11,599
We're already going through it.

569
00:23:11,839 --> 00:23:12,599
It's strictly compliant.

570
00:23:13,079 --> 00:23:13,599
As for this drug,

571
00:23:13,799 --> 00:23:15,279
there's really no problem with it.

572
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:17,079
The results are amazing.

573
00:23:19,839 --> 00:23:20,680
I've heard

574
00:23:20,799 --> 00:23:22,160
the Central Hospital in the next city

575
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,400
has already brought it in.

576
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,200
The feedback from specialists there

577
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,000
was overwhelmingly positive.

578
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,720
Even if the new director isn't decided,

579
00:23:28,039 --> 00:23:28,720
what drug gets approved

580
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,880
comes down to a stroke of your pen anyway.

581
00:23:30,079 --> 00:23:30,680
Besides,

582
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,720
the directorship is definitely yours.

583
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:33,359
Trust me.

584
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:34,079
My predictions

585
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:34,799
never fail.

586
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:37,039
Director Jin,

587
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,039
rest assured.

588
00:23:38,119 --> 00:23:39,039
As long as you

589
00:23:39,039 --> 00:23:39,799
give the word

590
00:23:40,079 --> 00:23:40,759
and start using it first,

591
00:23:41,319 --> 00:23:42,319
we all know the drill.

592
00:23:43,119 --> 00:23:44,559
We definitely won't let you do it for nothing.

593
00:23:45,039 --> 00:23:45,960
You'll be well taken care of.

594
00:23:46,119 --> 00:23:46,920
We'll see about that.

595
00:23:47,519 --> 00:23:49,799
Let's wait until the new director is chosen.

596
00:23:50,119 --> 00:23:51,000
Don't put me in a tough spot.

597
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,599
No problem, not at all.

598
00:23:57,039 --> 00:23:57,759
You're here, Jiayin.

599
00:23:57,759 --> 00:23:58,279
Where's Sister Feng?

600
00:23:58,559 --> 00:23:59,119
She's upstairs.

601
00:24:13,279 --> 00:24:13,680
Twenty thousand.

602
00:24:18,519 --> 00:24:19,559
Got the money, huh?

603
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,559
Finally wised up.

604
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,000
All these years,

605
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:23,880
things I didn't want to do,

606
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:24,799
I did them one after another.

607
00:24:25,359 --> 00:24:26,160
No matter how well I did,

608
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:27,839
nobody ever appreciated it.

609
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:28,880
Sister Feng, you're right.

610
00:24:29,319 --> 00:24:30,680
It's time I looked out for myself.

611
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,279
I need to do what I actually want.

612
00:24:32,839 --> 00:24:33,880
Even if I mess it up,

613
00:24:34,319 --> 00:24:35,359
it's my own choice.

614
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:36,759
Nobody can boss me around.

615
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:37,240
Good.

616
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:38,799
Look at you standing tall!

617
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:41,680
Though this doesn't look like enough.

618
00:24:41,799 --> 00:24:42,680
Consider it a deposit then.

619
00:24:44,039 --> 00:24:45,079
What about the rest of the money?

620
00:24:45,279 --> 00:24:46,480
Will your father-in-law agree to this?

621
00:24:46,519 --> 00:24:47,839
Write me a receipt first.

622
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:49,839
Nothing's hard once you start.

623
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:51,400
It's already in motion.

624
00:24:51,920 --> 00:24:53,039
We'll cross that bridge when we come to it.

625
00:24:54,119 --> 00:24:55,119
I thought

626
00:24:55,359 --> 00:24:57,559
you'd let the Sais walk all over you forever.

627
00:24:58,400 --> 00:25:00,039
But let's make things clear upfront.

628
00:25:00,319 --> 00:25:01,440
This is a deposit.

629
00:25:01,599 --> 00:25:02,599
Within two weeks,

630
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:04,240
if you don't pay the balance,

631
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:05,319
this money

632
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:06,400
is mine to keep.

633
00:25:06,440 --> 00:25:07,920
Alright, it's a deal.

634
00:25:11,359 --> 00:25:11,960
Sister Feng,

635
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:14,359
make sure you keep a good eye on the shop for me.

636
00:25:15,039 --> 00:25:15,960
Starting today,

637
00:25:16,799 --> 00:25:17,680
this shop belongs to the Sais!

638
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:20,000
The Sais?

639
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:21,759
Wen.

640
00:25:23,319 --> 00:25:23,920
It belongs to Wen now!

641
00:25:24,359 --> 00:25:25,400
Alright, Boss Wen.

642
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:31,000
From now on, this shop is mine!

643
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:32,839
Sister Wen took over the shop!

644
00:25:32,839 --> 00:25:33,960
Did you hear what she said?

645
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:34,759
She really pulled it off.

646
00:25:35,559 --> 00:25:36,960
She actually took over the shop!

647
00:25:49,039 --> 00:25:49,759
Ms. Sai,

648
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:51,480
I've reviewed your resume.

649
00:25:51,839 --> 00:25:53,200
After graduating from vocational school,

650
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:54,359
you worked for two years,

651
00:25:54,519 --> 00:25:55,400
then quit to stay home.

652
00:25:55,640 --> 00:25:56,759
May I ask...

653
00:25:57,240 --> 00:25:57,759
It's been seven years.

654
00:25:57,759 --> 00:25:58,319
Why...

655
00:25:58,559 --> 00:25:59,960
do you suddenly want to work again?

656
00:26:01,079 --> 00:26:01,559
Well...

657
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:02,880
Because...

658
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:06,200
things changed at home,

659
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:09,079
and I feel people need to earn their own living.

660
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:10,720
For this position,

661
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,319
it requires design,

662
00:26:12,839 --> 00:26:14,279
layout, and image-text processing.

663
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:16,359
Do you have relevant experience?

664
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:18,480
No,

665
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,519
but I can learn.

666
00:26:19,519 --> 00:26:21,000
I'm a fast learner.

667
00:26:23,839 --> 00:26:25,079
All right, Ms. Sai.

668
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,480
Thank you for coming in today.

669
00:26:27,079 --> 00:26:28,200
We'll be in touch.

670
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:29,359
Thank you.

671
00:26:30,559 --> 00:26:31,200
Call the next one in.

672
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:35,240
I... I don't stand a chance,

673
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:35,720
do I?

674
00:26:37,279 --> 00:26:37,920
Ms. Sai,

675
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:41,240
I saw the address on your ID.

676
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:42,279
You're from Qingyangli Village, right?

677
00:26:42,519 --> 00:26:43,960
Didn't that village just get demolished?

678
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:45,839
With more payout money than you could spend,

679
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:47,960
why rush to find a job?

680
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,720
Your resume says you're married,

681
00:26:50,119 --> 00:26:50,880
and your husband

682
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:51,920
is a doctor at the municipal hospital.

683
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:53,160
Honestly, it's not worth the trouble.

684
00:26:54,160 --> 00:26:55,039
There's really no need.

685
00:26:57,160 --> 00:26:58,480
Th-Thank you. Thank you.

686
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,319
Fix this formatting in a bit.

687
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:08,759
To further strengthen

688
00:27:09,279 --> 00:27:10,440
our hospital's Heart Center,

689
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:12,599
especially in cardiac surgery,

690
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,200
boost our scientific competitiveness,

691
00:27:14,519 --> 00:27:15,440
and better serve our patients,

692
00:27:16,359 --> 00:27:18,319
following careful deliberation by the Party committee

693
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,000
and approval from higher authorities,

694
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:22,640
we are deeply honored

695
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:24,039
to bring on board

696
00:27:24,279 --> 00:27:27,440
a highly accomplished

697
00:27:28,119 --> 00:27:29,160
young cardiac surgery specialist,

698
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:30,160
Lin Hong.

699
00:27:42,200 --> 00:27:43,359
What's going on with you?

700
00:27:43,759 --> 00:27:44,680
What do you mean, "what's going on"?

701
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:45,440
I'm completely exhausted.

702
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:46,440
I just got out of surgery.

703
00:27:47,559 --> 00:27:48,680
The hospital director already made the announcement,

704
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:49,839
everyone was applauding,

705
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:50,839
and you don't even know what happened?

706
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:51,759
What happened?

707
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:53,519
Look over there.

708
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:54,200
Who is that?

709
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,079
At the German Heart Center Berlin...

710
00:27:56,079 --> 00:27:56,480
Who?

711
00:27:57,119 --> 00:27:57,759
Lin Hong.

712
00:27:57,920 --> 00:27:58,799
Who's Lin Hong?

713
00:27:59,519 --> 00:28:00,880
Our department's new director.

714
00:28:01,119 --> 00:28:03,599
He trained under an international cardiac surgery authority,

715
00:28:04,279 --> 00:28:05,880
Professor John James.

716
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,440
You're completely out of the running now.

717
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:11,759
The director and secretary recruited him from Beijing.

718
00:28:12,319 --> 00:28:13,319
He brought along with him

719
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,759
tens of millions in major projects and top-tier papers.

720
00:28:16,079 --> 00:28:17,039
He didn't come here

721
00:28:17,279 --> 00:28:18,599
to compete with you.

722
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:20,160
He came to lead.

723
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:21,680
Especially in

724
00:28:22,359 --> 00:28:23,480
heart transplant

725
00:28:24,160 --> 00:28:25,480
perioperative management

726
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:27,519
and long-term outcome optimization,

727
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:31,160
he didn't just achieve Asia's first...

728
00:28:41,839 --> 00:28:42,400
Let me take this call.

729
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:50,240
Where's my yogurt?

730
00:29:50,559 --> 00:29:51,440
Where did you put it?

731
00:29:54,079 --> 00:29:55,240
I'm asking you, where is my yogurt?

732
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:55,680
There was so much of it.

733
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:56,599
Did you drink it all?

734
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:06,799
Why did you throw out my yogurt?

735
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:12,720
I'm asking why you threw my yogurt away!

736
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,839
What's going on? What's wrong?

737
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:18,640
The yogurt!

738
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:19,319
It was perfectly fine!

739
00:30:19,319 --> 00:30:20,519
Why did you throw it out?

740
00:30:20,920 --> 00:30:21,599
It's expired.

741
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:23,880
I don't understand!

742
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:24,839
Why did you throw it away?

743
00:30:25,279 --> 00:30:25,640
No...

744
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:26,359
It was all perfectly fine!

745
00:30:26,359 --> 00:30:27,200
Why did you throw it out?

746
00:30:27,279 --> 00:30:27,799
You threw it all away!

747
00:30:27,799 --> 00:30:28,559
It's expired.

748
00:30:28,559 --> 00:30:29,079
Look at the date here.

749
00:30:29,079 --> 00:30:30,119
The shelf life is seven days.

750
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,119
And look at the date here.

751
00:30:31,119 --> 00:30:31,920
It's expired.

752
00:30:31,920 --> 00:30:32,960
It's already day eight.

753
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:34,319
It's expired today.

754
00:30:34,359 --> 00:30:35,799
Yesterday was the seventh day.

755
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,039
So it's expired.

756
00:30:37,039 --> 00:30:38,480
It was only good until yesterday.

757
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:39,839
It's only been one day!

758
00:30:39,839 --> 00:30:40,400
Listen to me.

759
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:40,960
Just one day!

760
00:30:41,039 --> 00:30:41,680
But it's still expired!

761
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:42,680
It's drinkable. It's totally fine!

762
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:44,240
No, you'll get diarrhea and a stomachache!

763
00:30:44,240 --> 00:30:44,920
It doesn't matter!

764
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:45,640
I'm telling you...

765
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:46,720
I'll prove it to you!

766
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:47,400
It's fine.

767
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:56,720
It's completely drinkable!

768
00:30:56,720 --> 00:30:57,960
Oh, my god!

769
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:58,440
It's totally fine!

770
00:30:58,440 --> 00:30:59,039
Don't drink it!

771
00:30:59,160 --> 00:31:00,079
You can't drink that!

772
00:31:00,079 --> 00:31:01,119
Yes, I can. It won't kill me!

773
00:31:01,119 --> 00:31:02,000
You can't drink that!

774
00:31:02,079 --> 00:31:03,039
Watch me drink it. Come on!

775
00:31:03,039 --> 00:31:03,319
No!

776
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,319
Just watch me drink it!

777
00:31:04,359 --> 00:31:04,759
No, no, no!

778
00:31:04,759 --> 00:31:05,480
Here, just watch!

779
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:06,359
It's gone bad!

780
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:06,920
It's fine!

781
00:31:07,079 --> 00:31:07,440
No!

782
00:31:09,279 --> 00:31:10,279
No, you can't drink that!

783
00:31:10,279 --> 00:31:11,200
Let me finish it!

784
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:32,160
Are you tired from last night?

785
00:31:32,599 --> 00:31:32,960
I'm fine.

786
00:31:34,279 --> 00:31:34,599
Dad.

787
00:31:35,240 --> 00:31:35,839
Son.

788
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:38,079
How are you feeling?

789
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:39,559
No discomfort, right?

790
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:42,599
You've lost weight.

791
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:43,799
No, I haven't.

792
00:31:44,799 --> 00:31:45,599
The site...

793
00:31:46,599 --> 00:31:47,640
Everything's fine.

794
00:31:48,119 --> 00:31:48,720
At the site...

795
00:31:49,319 --> 00:31:49,839
It's doing okay.

796
00:31:50,759 --> 00:31:51,279
Dad, speaking of which,

797
00:31:51,559 --> 00:31:52,759
about the construction site...

798
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:53,440
Dad,

799
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:54,240
I wanted to discuss something with you.

800
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:55,039
You must be hungry, right?

801
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:57,599
Xiuming,

802
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,440
let's go see what food there is

803
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:00,200
and get some for Dad.

804
00:32:00,759 --> 00:32:02,000
He's had porridge for days.

805
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:04,279
The doctor said he can eat other things today.

806
00:32:04,759 --> 00:32:06,119
Okay, we'll buy it in a bit.

807
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:07,160
Let me finish talking with Dad first.

808
00:32:07,599 --> 00:32:07,920
Dad...

809
00:32:08,039 --> 00:32:09,359
I know what you want to say.

810
00:32:09,359 --> 00:32:10,559
I already told Dad.

811
00:32:11,079 --> 00:32:13,000
Zhenzhu's been busy studying these past couple of days,

812
00:32:13,119 --> 00:32:14,759
so she'll visit Grandpa in a few days.

813
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:16,240
It's not about Zhenzhu.

814
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:17,319
I'm talking about Xiuliang.

815
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:17,799
Dad...

816
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:19,200
Oh right, I just remembered!

817
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:20,039
Dad,

818
00:32:20,359 --> 00:32:21,480
what Xiuming meant was,

819
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,039
you know Xiuliang...

820
00:32:23,720 --> 00:32:25,680
he's been going to the site every day lately,

821
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:27,279
and managing the accounts quite clearly.

822
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:28,759
But you see,

823
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,920
doesn't he have his own business to run?

824
00:32:31,519 --> 00:32:32,960
Xiuming feels that juggling both

825
00:32:33,359 --> 00:32:34,119
is too much for him.

826
00:32:34,359 --> 00:32:35,640
So he wanted to ask you

827
00:32:35,759 --> 00:32:38,000
if Xiuliang could handle the major accounts,

828
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,039
while the petty, trivial expenses

829
00:32:40,039 --> 00:32:41,319
could be given to Qingyou

830
00:32:41,599 --> 00:32:42,599
or someone else,

831
00:32:43,400 --> 00:32:44,559
to help share his load.

832
00:32:46,039 --> 00:32:46,839
Son.

833
00:32:47,480 --> 00:32:47,799
Dad.

834
00:32:48,440 --> 00:32:50,319
Is that what you wanted to say?

835
00:32:53,599 --> 00:32:55,480
I just wanted to consult you

836
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:57,640
on what amount counts as

837
00:32:58,880 --> 00:32:59,640
a petty expense.

838
00:33:00,960 --> 00:33:02,000
What amount...

839
00:33:02,599 --> 00:33:05,119
You two brothers discuss and decide.

840
00:33:07,000 --> 00:33:08,720
You have to trust your brother.

841
00:33:10,079 --> 00:33:11,240
He knows what he's doing.

842
00:33:14,799 --> 00:33:15,079
Dad,

843
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:17,240
what would you like to eat?

844
00:33:17,599 --> 00:33:18,759
We'll go get it for you.

845
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:23,720
Xiuming!

846
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:26,039
Why are you walking so fast, Xiuming?

847
00:33:28,039 --> 00:33:29,000
What are you doing?

848
00:33:29,119 --> 00:33:29,880
What do you think I'm doing?

849
00:33:30,039 --> 00:33:30,960
What were you saying in the room?

850
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:32,559
What are you playing at?

851
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:33,880
What kind of stunt was that?

852
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:34,359
What?

853
00:33:34,359 --> 00:33:35,079
How old are you?

854
00:33:35,079 --> 00:33:35,839
Tattling at every turn.

855
00:33:35,839 --> 00:33:36,359
How was I tattling?

856
00:33:36,359 --> 00:33:36,920
I was winking at you.

857
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:37,880
Couldn't you take a hint?

858
00:33:37,880 --> 00:33:38,880
I had to talk serious business with Dad!

859
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:39,640
What serious business?

860
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:40,319
Dad just had surgery.

861
00:33:40,319 --> 00:33:41,079
Bringing this up to him now,

862
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:42,039
aren't you just stressing him out?

863
00:33:42,039 --> 00:33:42,519
If I don't say it now,

864
00:33:42,519 --> 00:33:43,440
when am I supposed to say it?

865
00:33:43,599 --> 00:33:44,079
If I keep quiet,

866
00:33:44,079 --> 00:33:45,400
the construction team won't survive!

867
00:33:52,240 --> 00:33:52,640
Guarding,

868
00:33:54,440 --> 00:33:55,119
guarding...

869
00:33:57,480 --> 00:33:58,640
Who is he guarding against all day?

870
00:34:01,079 --> 00:34:02,240
You think your dad doesn't know

871
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:03,559
that Xiuliang can't read the ledgers?

872
00:34:03,799 --> 00:34:04,759
Even so,

873
00:34:05,039 --> 00:34:06,640
he still won't give the books to you. Why?

874
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:08,039
He's guarding against me. You think I'm stupid?

875
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:18,800
Your dad has so much cunning,

876
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:20,719
why couldn't you get even a bit of it?

877
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:37,440
Mingming.

878
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:39,840
What is it?

879
00:34:40,760 --> 00:34:41,519
20mm rebar,

880
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:42,639
and 0.9 tie wire.

881
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:43,480
Buy them for me.

882
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:48,480
Brother, didn't we just buy some two days ago?

883
00:34:48,639 --> 00:34:49,119
Why buy more?

884
00:34:50,079 --> 00:34:51,360
I need the 20mm rebar!

885
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:53,760
Aren't there over 2,000 bars left outside?

886
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:55,159
Why... why do you need so many?

887
00:34:55,159 --> 00:34:56,280
None of your business what I need them for!

888
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:57,199
The 0.9 tie wire,

889
00:34:57,199 --> 00:34:57,880
buy it for me right now!

890
00:34:58,039 --> 00:34:58,920
I need it today!

891
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:00,800
We can't just blow through our money like this!

892
00:35:00,920 --> 00:35:01,800
Can you not make the call?

893
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:03,920
If you can't make the call,

894
00:35:04,119 --> 00:35:05,840
then call the person who can!

895
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:06,599
Did you hear me?

896
00:35:06,719 --> 00:35:07,440
He won't approve it.

897
00:35:11,440 --> 00:35:12,880
I don't care if he approves or not!

898
00:35:13,119 --> 00:35:14,679
I need it today!

899
00:35:14,679 --> 00:35:15,360
You hear me?

900
00:35:15,840 --> 00:35:16,280
Make the call!

901
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:19,639
Well, I...

902
00:35:19,639 --> 00:35:20,320
Call right here.

903
00:35:20,639 --> 00:35:21,599
Right here!

904
00:35:21,679 --> 00:35:22,400
Call right in front of me!

905
00:35:28,559 --> 00:35:29,559
Why are you texting?

906
00:35:29,559 --> 00:35:30,840
I told you to call him!

907
00:35:31,039 --> 00:35:31,960
It's not a good time for him.

908
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:33,159
Who cares if it's a good time?

909
00:35:33,280 --> 00:35:33,719
Call him!

910
00:35:36,280 --> 00:35:37,840
Mr. Shi, let me give you a quick briefing.

911
00:35:37,840 --> 00:35:38,920
Our recent work

912
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:39,920
is divided into two main parts.

913
00:35:40,360 --> 00:35:41,119
First,

914
00:35:41,119 --> 00:35:43,159
we reached out to Mr. Wei from Changfu

915
00:35:43,159 --> 00:35:45,519
for an initial informal discussion.

916
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:47,559
The purpose was to convey

917
00:35:48,119 --> 00:35:50,119
Tengyue's sincerity regarding this acquisition.

918
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:51,239
Second,

919
00:35:51,239 --> 00:35:53,639
we examined Changfu's public financial data

920
00:35:53,880 --> 00:35:55,519
and their track record on past projects.

921
00:35:55,719 --> 00:35:56,559
We conducted a full review,

922
00:35:57,559 --> 00:35:58,119
including...

923
00:36:01,599 --> 00:36:03,199
including asset evaluation

924
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,920
and staff placement.

925
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Our team has already prepared

926
00:36:07,199 --> 00:36:08,920
a draft of the framework document.

927
00:36:10,239 --> 00:36:11,360
See? He didn't pick up!

928
00:36:11,519 --> 00:36:12,800
Then keep calling until he does!

929
00:36:13,239 --> 00:36:14,119
I'm waiting right here.

930
00:36:14,480 --> 00:36:15,719
I'm not going anywhere. I'll wait!

931
00:36:23,039 --> 00:36:23,880
There's one more thing.

932
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:27,119
Regarding the Changfu Construction site,

933
00:36:27,119 --> 00:36:28,519
could the Phase 3 payment

934
00:36:30,119 --> 00:36:31,360
be eased up a bit,

935
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:33,440
and have part of it released?

936
00:36:34,159 --> 00:36:34,920
Mainly because

937
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:37,199
things are really tight on site.

938
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:38,679
The workers' wages,

939
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:40,000
plus final payments for materials...

940
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,840
If we don't disburse them soon,

941
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:43,039
I'm worried

942
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:45,480
work will grind to a near halt.

943
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,639
Ultimately, it'll affect

944
00:36:47,639 --> 00:36:49,400
our Tengyue project as a whole.

945
00:36:49,440 --> 00:36:50,360
Take your call first.

946
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:54,360
Excuse me.

947
00:37:01,039 --> 00:37:01,440
Go ahead.

948
00:37:02,239 --> 00:37:02,800
Brother Liang,

949
00:37:03,519 --> 00:37:04,840
got something to report.

950
00:37:05,119 --> 00:37:06,920
This time, I still need

951
00:37:07,199 --> 00:37:08,400
size 20 rebar,

952
00:37:08,599 --> 00:37:09,239
three batches,

953
00:37:09,639 --> 00:37:11,039
paid in three installments.

954
00:37:11,360 --> 00:37:12,639
Could you authorize it?

955
00:37:12,639 --> 00:37:13,039
All right?

956
00:37:13,239 --> 00:37:13,599
Hold on.

957
00:37:14,280 --> 00:37:15,159
Why three installments?

958
00:37:15,320 --> 00:37:15,960
Different manufacturers?

959
00:37:16,559 --> 00:37:17,119
They're the same.

960
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:20,000
Different prices, then?

961
00:37:20,719 --> 00:37:21,360
The same too.

962
00:37:21,559 --> 00:37:23,000
Then why three installments?

963
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:23,760
Not approved.

964
00:37:24,159 --> 00:37:24,519
Fine.

965
00:37:24,719 --> 00:37:25,920
Let's set that aside for now.

966
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:29,079
For the 0.9 mm binding wire,

967
00:37:29,559 --> 00:37:31,039
I need another 100 meters.

968
00:37:31,360 --> 00:37:32,119
The nylon one.

969
00:37:33,039 --> 00:37:34,519
Didn't I approve that a few days ago?

970
00:37:35,039 --> 00:37:37,000
Last time was 0.4 mm nylon cable ties.

971
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,000
Those are for temporary binding.

972
00:37:38,599 --> 00:37:39,719
This 0.9 mm...

973
00:37:40,119 --> 00:37:41,000
this binding wire,

974
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,440
it's rust-resistant concrete tie wire.

975
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:46,000
It's for moisture-proofing in the basement.

976
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:46,519
Stop, stop, stop.

977
00:37:47,719 --> 00:37:49,480
I remember approving this one too.

978
00:37:50,159 --> 00:37:50,920
Used up already?

979
00:37:51,679 --> 00:37:52,280
Not used up.

980
00:37:53,039 --> 00:37:53,519
Not used up?

981
00:37:53,519 --> 00:37:54,360
Then why buy more?

982
00:37:55,400 --> 00:37:56,280
He asked for it!

983
00:37:56,599 --> 00:37:58,079
Just authorize it,

984
00:37:58,079 --> 00:37:58,480
approve it,

985
00:37:58,480 --> 00:37:59,800
and let me buy it, will you?

986
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:00,320
Denied.

987
00:38:03,679 --> 00:38:04,519
He won't approve it.

988
00:38:05,519 --> 00:38:06,159
Won't approve it, huh?

989
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:08,960
If the project gets delayed,

990
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:09,719
it's on you.

991
00:38:09,960 --> 00:38:10,880
If you can't take responsibility,

992
00:38:11,400 --> 00:38:12,719
get someone who can.

993
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:13,679
Or just call him.

994
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,320
Keep calling.

995
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:27,400
Sorry about that.

996
00:38:28,119 --> 00:38:29,360
Just some minor issues at the construction site.

997
00:38:29,719 --> 00:38:30,400
Let's continue.

998
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:33,400
Lawyer Sai.

999
00:38:34,079 --> 00:38:35,960
Let's talk about the phase three payment first.

1000
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:39,880
I believe that on this issue,

1001
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:41,079
we previously reached a basic consensus.

1002
00:38:41,599 --> 00:38:42,159
That's fine.

1003
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:43,679
Let me reiterate my view.

1004
00:38:44,239 --> 00:38:45,800
Acquiring Changfu

1005
00:38:46,159 --> 00:38:47,360
isn't just about a project or two,

1006
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:49,239
but part of the group's overall

1007
00:38:49,599 --> 00:38:50,800
development strategy in Honggang.

1008
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:51,400
Of course,

1009
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:52,599
with reforms,

1010
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:53,960
there will inevitably be growing pains.

1011
00:38:54,639 --> 00:38:55,960
Some of the things we're doing now

1012
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:58,280
may seem harsh and cold-hearted,

1013
00:38:58,639 --> 00:39:00,599
but cutting the Gordian knot

1014
00:39:01,119 --> 00:39:02,400
actually paves the way for the future.

1015
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:03,960
By doing this,

1016
00:39:04,199 --> 00:39:05,559
I'm actually helping them,

1017
00:39:05,719 --> 00:39:06,840
as well as ourselves.

1018
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:07,840
Don't you think what I'm saying

1019
00:39:07,960 --> 00:39:08,800
makes sense?

1020
00:39:09,079 --> 00:39:10,079
I understand what you mean.

1021
00:39:10,320 --> 00:39:12,599
I'm just worried that applying too much pressure

1022
00:39:12,679 --> 00:39:14,199
and pulling the string too tight

1023
00:39:14,199 --> 00:39:15,599
will only lead to a deadlock,

1024
00:39:16,079 --> 00:39:16,960
and the final outcome—

1025
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:17,639
I get it.

1026
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:19,360
I completely understand

1027
00:39:19,360 --> 00:39:20,400
your difficulties as a mediator

1028
00:39:20,519 --> 00:39:22,239
in trying to coordinate all of this.

1029
00:39:23,360 --> 00:39:24,039
But what choice do we have?

1030
00:39:24,880 --> 00:39:27,039
We're the ones sitting in these positions,

1031
00:39:27,360 --> 00:39:29,239
so there are decisions we have to make.

1032
00:39:29,639 --> 00:39:30,639
The group entrusted this task

1033
00:39:30,719 --> 00:39:31,920
to both you and me.

1034
00:39:32,599 --> 00:39:33,400
On one hand, it's trust,

1035
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:34,679
and on the other,

1036
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:35,719
it's a test.

1037
00:39:43,239 --> 00:39:44,119
Look, Lawyer Sai.

1038
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:46,480
If you feel this matter

1039
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:47,519
is too difficult to handle

1040
00:39:47,679 --> 00:39:48,719
or too complicated,

1041
00:39:49,159 --> 00:39:49,519
that's fine.

1042
00:39:50,079 --> 00:39:50,719
Just let me know early.

1043
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:52,760
We can always explore other options

1044
00:39:53,760 --> 00:39:55,800
and see what alternative routes we can take.

1045
00:39:56,119 --> 00:39:56,360
Fine.

1046
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:56,760
Right?

1047
00:39:57,079 --> 00:39:58,280
But in any case, remember this:

1048
00:39:59,119 --> 00:39:59,800
the project won't wait,

1049
00:40:00,599 --> 00:40:01,480
and neither will the market.

1050
00:40:04,199 --> 00:40:04,840
Is there anything else?

1051
00:40:05,119 --> 00:40:06,400
Nothing from our side.

1052
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:08,119
Meeting adjourned.

1053
00:40:28,960 --> 00:40:30,280
Are you people out of your minds?

1054
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:31,400
You did this on purpose, didn't you?

1055
00:40:32,719 --> 00:40:33,440
It wasn't us.

1056
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,320
I'm the one stirring up trouble.

1057
00:40:36,559 --> 00:40:37,360
Put him on the phone.

1058
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:41,079
Answer it.

1059
00:40:45,519 --> 00:40:46,079
He won't take it.

1060
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:47,199
Then tell him

1061
00:40:47,199 --> 00:40:48,440
to wait for me at the construction site.

1062
00:40:50,599 --> 00:40:52,880
Brother-in-law, is there really no chance with Changfu?

1063
00:40:54,639 --> 00:40:55,559
Then what are we supposed to do?

1064
00:40:56,199 --> 00:40:56,840
Besides, Tengyue

1065
00:40:56,840 --> 00:40:58,320
won't listen to all our excuses.

1066
00:41:00,639 --> 00:41:01,280
You head back first.

1067
00:41:01,280 --> 00:41:01,840
I need to step out.

1068
00:41:02,559 --> 00:41:02,960
Car keys.

1069
00:41:03,519 --> 00:41:03,880
Right here.

1070
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:21,719
Big Brother.

1071
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:23,559
What's wrong? What happened?

1072
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:24,840
Nothing's happened yet.

1073
00:41:25,639 --> 00:41:26,920
Though trouble might start soon.

1074
00:41:29,159 --> 00:41:29,880
Did you call him over?

1075
00:41:31,159 --> 00:41:31,800
Nice work.

1076
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:33,440
Just love stirring up drama, don't you?

1077
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:34,000
Was it you?

1078
00:41:34,119 --> 00:41:35,000
You lot...

1079
00:41:35,639 --> 00:41:36,840
I'm done dealing with you all.

1080
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:38,320
None of you listen to me, do you?

1081
00:41:38,639 --> 00:41:40,400
Just determined to ruin a good life, aren't you?

1082
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:42,679
Go talk some sense into him.

1083
00:41:43,320 --> 00:41:44,159
Try to reason with him.

1084
00:41:44,320 --> 00:41:44,880
Fine, I got it.

1085
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:45,440
Go on back.

1086
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:48,679
What's that supposed to mean, Big Brother?

1087
00:41:51,119 --> 00:41:52,599
Fine by me, I love watching the drama.

1088
00:41:55,239 --> 00:41:56,159
Listen, on a serious note.

1089
00:41:56,320 --> 00:41:57,320
I just heard on the street

1090
00:41:57,519 --> 00:41:58,960
that Ma the Third is trying to sell his crew.

1091
00:41:59,000 --> 00:41:59,679
Pay closer attention.

1092
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:00,400
Don't let things go sideways.

1093
00:42:00,679 --> 00:42:02,199
You're still worrying about the Mas?

1094
00:42:03,800 --> 00:42:04,440
At this rate,

1095
00:42:04,800 --> 00:42:05,599
our own construction crew

1096
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:07,400
might get sold before theirs!

1097
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:07,880
You know that?

1098
00:42:08,039 --> 00:42:09,159
Right now, the boss won't show,

1099
00:42:09,159 --> 00:42:10,599
and I can't get a single penny.

1100
00:42:10,719 --> 00:42:11,280
If I don't get paid,

1101
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:12,000
we stop working.

1102
00:42:12,079 --> 00:42:12,800
Shut it down!

1103
00:42:13,480 --> 00:42:14,239
Why even bother working?

1104
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:16,480
Wait, why are you taking it out on me?

1105
00:42:22,480 --> 00:42:22,880
All right, that's enough.

1106
00:42:23,480 --> 00:42:24,280
Cool off for a second.

1107
00:42:25,159 --> 00:42:26,239
I just don't get it.

1108
00:42:26,599 --> 00:42:28,039
Big Brother, you don't want Second Brother in charge,

1109
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:29,840
and Second Brother doesn't want to run it either.

1110
00:42:30,079 --> 00:42:31,280
So what are you two fighting over?

1111
00:42:31,440 --> 00:42:32,519
Isn't this the old man's fault?

1112
00:42:32,519 --> 00:42:33,719
Go take it out on the old man!

1113
00:42:33,800 --> 00:42:34,559
That's between the two of us.

1114
00:42:35,239 --> 00:42:36,159
Keep your nose out of it.

1115
00:42:58,960 --> 00:42:59,559
Where's Yang Qingyou?

1116
00:43:00,599 --> 00:43:01,039
He ran off.

1117
00:43:01,719 --> 00:43:02,679
I'm the only one left watching the show.

1118
00:43:04,559 --> 00:43:05,159
What else do you need to buy?

1119
00:43:05,159 --> 00:43:05,920
Spell it out for me.

1120
00:43:05,920 --> 00:43:06,719
Tell me everything once and for all.

1121
00:43:06,800 --> 00:43:07,559
The 20mm rebar...

1122
00:43:07,559 --> 00:43:08,360
Why buy it in three batches?

1123
00:43:08,360 --> 00:43:09,280
Why did he give you the ledger?

1124
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:10,519
Why did Dad give you the ledger?

1125
00:43:10,639 --> 00:43:11,199
Who's he guarding against?

1126
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:20,599
Show me some respect.

1127
00:43:20,599 --> 00:43:21,480
Wherever I work,

1128
00:43:21,559 --> 00:43:22,280
go wait for me there.

1129
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:23,039
Without my signature,

1130
00:43:23,119 --> 00:43:24,400
you won't get a single cent.

1131
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:25,000
That's final.

1132
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:25,639
You stay right here!

1133
00:43:25,840 --> 00:43:26,079
You...

1134
00:43:26,519 --> 00:43:26,920
Go!

1135
